(1. Objective Clearance vs Chronological Time) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(Chronological time alone \(>9-12 months\) is necessary for biological graft ligamentisation but insufficient for discharge.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(Safe return to sport requires meeting comprehensive objective neuromuscular, functional, and psychological criteria.) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(2. The 10 Objective Return-to-Play Criteria) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(1. Full active knee extension \(0 degrees\) and symmetrical flexion with zero persistent effusion or joint warmth.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(2. Quadriceps strength Limb Symmetry Index \(LSI\) > 90% \(preferably >100% on isokinetic testing\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(3. Single-leg hop battery \(single hop, triple hop, crossover hop, 6m timed hop\) demonstrating LSI > 90%.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(4. Qualitative movement assessment: elimination of dynamic knee valgus and trunk collapse on jump landing.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(5. Reactive agility and multidirectional deceleration mechanics evaluated under high-speed video recording.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(6. High psychological readiness verified via ACL-RSI questionnaire \(validated cut-off score > 65\).) Tj
0 -24 Td
/F1 7.5 Tf
